{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790988427,"nonce":"0ckw4pCTQDDzVT+LNeIkvRFf0Vw=","title":"SVG rendering, parsed in Haxe","message":"SVG is parsed on the Haxe side with Haxe's own XML support, not by blinc_svg's parser.\n\n- Inline `\u003csvg\u003e` in an hxx template: the hxx macro parses the markup at compile time into typed path data (move/line/cubic/quad/arc/close, fill, stroke, transform, viewBox). A malformed icon is a compile error at its own position.\n- SVG from a string or file at run time: `Xml.parse` into the same typed model.\n- The typed model is the one thing both routes produce, so styling (fill from a theme colour, `currentColor` from the text colour) binds the same way either way.\n\nRasterization goes through Blinc for speed, as text does: the parsed paths cross blinc_abi once per shape and size, rasterized at on-screen size (display scale times transform scale, bucketed) into an RGBA atlas that ashui's own hxsl shader samples. This keeps zoomed icons crisp, unlike a fixed-size bitmap.\n\nFollows text rendering (e532fc0), which builds the atlas, upload and glyph pass this reuses.","files":null}]}